## ARTICLE VII: HEALTHCARE AND INSURANCE

### Section 7.1: Non-Discrimination in Healthcare

**7.1.1** No healthcare entity may discriminate on the basis of augmentation status.

**7.1.2** Healthcare services shall be accessible to augmented citizens.

**7.1.3** Diagnostic procedures shall be compatible with augmentations.

**7.1.4** Surgical care shall respect augmentations.

**7.1.5** Emergency care shall accommodate assistive technology.

### Section 7.2: Non-Discrimination in Insurance

**7.2.1** No insurance provider may discriminate on the basis of augmentation status.

**7.2.2** Coverage shall not be denied, limited, or priced differently because of augmentation.

**7.2.3** Actuarial justification may be required for differential treatment.

**7.2.4** No individual shall be required to deactivate augmentations as a condition of coverage.

### Section 7.3: Healthcare Accessibility

**7.3.1** Healthcare facilities shall be accessible to augmented citizens.

**7.3.2** Healthcare providers shall receive training on augmentations.

**7.3.3** Healthcare information shall be accessible.

**7.3.4** Healthcare decisions shall respect the autonomy of augmented citizens.

