## ARTICLE XVIII: SEVERABILITY AND SUPREMACY

### Section 18.1: Severability

**18.1.1** If any provision of this Constitution is held invalid, the remainder shall continue.

**18.1.2** If any application is held invalid, other applications shall continue.

**18.1.3** The invalidity of a provision shall not affect related provisions.

**18.1.4** The intent of this Constitution shall be preserved.

### Section 18.2: Supremacy

**18.2.1** This Constitution is the supreme governing document of the Augmented-Hub.

**18.2.2** All policies, regulations, and decisions shall be consistent with this Constitution.

**18.2.3** In case of conflict, this Constitution shall prevail.

**18.2.4** This Constitution shall be interpreted broadly to protect augmented rights.

### Section 18.3: Implementation

**18.3.1** This Constitution shall be implemented in good faith.

**18.3.2** Entities shall take all necessary steps to comply.

**18.3.3** Implementation shall be monitored and enforced.

**18.3.4** Progress shall be reported and reviewed.

---

## ARTICLE XIX: RIGHTS PRECEDENCE

### Section 19.1: Precedence of Rights

**19.1.1** In case of conflict between rights, precedence shall be determined by the following hierarchy:

| **Priority** | **Right** |
|--------------|-----------|
| 1 | Dignity and Equal Treatment |
| 2 | Privacy and Data Sovereignty |
| 3 | Accessibility and Assistive Necessity |
| 4 | Continuity and Identity Neutrality |
| 5 | Autonomy and Revocable Consent |
| 6 | Participation and Expression |
| 7 | Wellbeing and Happiness |
| 8 | Transparency and Accountability |
| 9 | Ecological Responsibility |

**19.1.2** No right may be used to justify the violation of a higher-priority right.

**19.1.3** Rights precedence shall be considered in all decisions.

**19.1.4** Rights precedence shall be reviewed and updated as needed.

### Section 19.2: Balancing Rights

**19.2.1** Rights shall be balanced in good faith.

**19.2.2** Balancing shall consider:
- The nature and purpose of the rights
- The context of the decision
- The impact on individuals
- The public interest

**19.2.3** Balancing shall be documented and justified.

**19.2.4** Balancing shall be subject to review.

